==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sauːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|auːr|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|sárr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|sairaz|lang=gem-pro}}.

====Adjective====
{{is-adj-01|sár|sárt|sárari|sárastur}}

# [[painful]], [[sore]]{{jump|is|painful|s}}
#: ''Á! Þetta er '''sárt'''!''
#:: Ouch! This '''hurts'''!
# [[bitter]], [[distressing]]{{jump|is|distressing|s}}
# [[hurt]], [[offended]], [[embittered]]{{jump|is|embittered|s}}

=====Inflection=====
{{is-decl-adj-1|s|á|r}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[eiga um sárt að binda]] (to have suffered a great loss)
* [[sitja eftir með sárt ennið]] (to be sorely disappointed)
* [[mig tekur það sárt]] (I'm really sorry)
* [[vera sárt leikinn]] (to be treated roughly)
* [[vera sárt um]] (to set great store by something)

=====Synonyms=====
* {{jump|s|is|painful}} [[kvalafullur]]
* {{jump|s|is|distressing}} [[átakanlegur]]
* {{jump|s|is|embittered}} [[gramur]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|sár|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|sairą|lang=gem-pro}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|n|sárs|sár}}

# a [[wound]]{{jump|is|wound|s}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s|s|á|r}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[fótasár]] (venous ulcers, stasis ulcer, varicose ulcers)
* [[gera að sárum]] (to dress somebody's wounds)
* [[græða sár]] (to heal a wound)
* [[vera í sárum]] (to moult)

=====Synonyms=====
* {{jump|s|is|wound}} {{qualifier|poetic}} [[und]]

